  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "[\"Original genus-level target is fulfilled by a named complete fossil specimen interpretation, not a living reconstruction. Preserve damaged lip boundary; do not restore missing shell.\", \"The original narrow angular rim is represented by real blunt-edged convergent geometry, without exaggerating it into a knife edge.\", \"Opposite lateral surface is not directly photographed here; infer approximate bilateral shell symmetry conservatively, without inventing different anatomy or repeating damage as exact bilateral features.\", \"No precise suture reconstruction or trace of unobserved inner chambers. Mineral-filled terminal face and shallow umbilical recess only.\"] {\"unit\": \"metre\", \"maximum_diameter\": 0.22, \"in_plane_width\": 0.188, \"maximum_axial_thickness\": 0.063, \"umbilical_depression_outer_diameter\": 0.027, \"central_recess_diameter\": 0.012, \"basis\": \"Plate18 caption explicitly gives specimen diameter220mm. Lateral width/height and ventral breadth estimated visually from the same published photos: width about0.85D, total thickness about0.28–0.30D. These secondary measurements are approximate, not caliper measurements.\", \"uncertainty\": \"About10–15% for photo-derived proportions; retain actual moderately compressed lenticular fossil instead of artificially thinning to satisfy an adjective.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：[\"Original genus-level target is fulfilled by a named complete fossil specimen interpretation, not a living reconstruction. Preserve damaged lip boundary; do not restore missing shell.\", \"The original narrow angular rim is represented by real blunt-edged convergent geometry, without exaggerating it into a knife edge.\", \"Opposite lateral surface is not directly photographed here; infer approximate bilateral shell symmetry conservatively, without inventing different anatomy or repeating damage as exact bilateral features.\", \"No precise suture reconstruction or trace of unobserved inner chambers. Mineral-filled terminal face and shallow umbilical recess only.\"] {\"unit\": \"metre\", \"maximum_diameter\": 0.22, \"in_plane_width\": 0.188, \"maximum_axial_thickness\": 0.063, \"umbilical_depression_outer_diameter\": 0.027, \"central_recess_diameter\": 0.012, \"basis\": \"Plate18 caption explicitly gives specimen diameter220mm. Lateral width/height and ventral breadth estimated visually from the same published photos: width about0.85D, total thickness about0.28–0.30D. These secondary measurements are approximate, not caliper measurements.\", \"uncertainty\": \"About10–15% for photo-derived proportions; retain actual moderately compressed lenticular fossil instead of artificially thinning to satisfy an adjective.\"}"
  },
